<p>I started with HTML and CSS over 10 years ago and spent most of my career building large-scale React apps.
  Accessibility, performance and a strong foundation in the basics are still part of everything I build. Over time, I
  moved across the whole stack. Today I deliver features end to end (front-end and Kotlin backend) on our Reference Data
  Management product at Ataccama.</p>

<p>Aside from product work, I lead our AI circle &mdash; an initiative to re-invent how our engineering organization
  builds software with AI. Generating code is the easy part. The hard part is knowing the output is correct and
  maintainable, so I spend my time on agentic harnesses, skills, evals and quality gates. For example, my
  <a href="https://github.com/Pustelto/code-review-skills">code review skill</a> ranks 2nd of 44 tools on the Martian
  Code Review Bench.</p>

<p>I have also built two solo products, <a href="https://clipio.app">Clipio</a> and Qjub. I drove everything from market
  research and design to backend, payments and marketing. Neither became a sustainable business, but both pushed me far
  outside my comfort zone (and taught me more than any course would).</p>

<p>In addition to my work, I enjoy spending time with my family (I'm a father of three boys) and hobbies such as being
  in nature, reading, and enjoying great tea. I'm also a great productivity and tooling geek.</p>

